# A token's copiable values are the characteristics the effect that made it defined (CR 111.4, 707.2; the card's ruling),
# and being a token is not one of them. On turn 1 Bot1 casts Lingering Souls for two 1/1 white Spirit creature tokens
# with flying, then Clone, copying the first: the Clone is a Spirit named Spirit, a white 1/1 Creature - Spirit with
# flying and no mana cost, and a card, not a token.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Lingering Souls
Clone
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Lingering Souls.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Spirit Token#1.Token = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Clone.Cast
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Target(Spirit Token)
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 1
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Spirit Token; Spirit Token; Spirit Token
Bot1.Battlefield.Spirit Token#3.Token = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Spirit Token#3.Types = Creature
Bot1.Battlefield.Spirit Token#3.Subtypes = Spirit
Bot1.Battlefield.Spirit Token#3.Colors = White
Bot1.Battlefield.Spirit Token#3.Keywords = Flying
Bot1.Battlefield.Spirit Token#3.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Spirit Token#3.Toughness = 1
Bot1.Graveyard = Black Lotus; Lingering Souls; Black Lotus
